# Why: upstream #77100 (CLOSED, NOT merged) -- a cron standalone delivery runs
# `asyncio.run()` on a fresh loop in the scheduler thread. send_message's Matrix
# live-adapter path then awaits the gateway-bound mautrix/aiohttp session from a
# DIFFERENT loop, so aiohttp's TimerContext raises "Timeout context manager should
# be used inside a task" and every scheduled Matrix delivery fails. Falling back to
# an ephemeral adapter instead re-inits E2EE and hits BAD_ACCOUNT_KEY on the shared
# crypto store (#46310), so the send must be SCHEDULED onto the adapter's own loop.
#
# RE-ANCHORED on the v0.23.2 bump: upstream moved
#   tools/send_message_senders.py -> gateway/outbound/senders.py
# (send.py keeps the tool entrypoint, senders.py the per-platform senders). Two
# context hunks apply unchanged; the import/logic hunks were re-derived from the
# tagged file. The move also exposed a latent bug in the v0.23.1 form of this
# patch: senders.py does NOT import asyncio, so `asyncio.get_running_loop()` raised
# NameError inside _matrix_adapter_loop_matches()'s try/except and the helper
# silently returned True (legacy direct await) -- the bridge was dead code. This
# revision adds `import asyncio` explicitly.
#
# Keep until #77100 or an equivalent loop check merges upstream.

